<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent, never LaunchDaemon: fld reads ~/.claude and talks to
  the user's tmux sockets — per-user work that must run as the user, not root.

  No app bundle, no code signing, no TCC prompt: nothing fld does in P0-P2
  touches an Automation-gated API. ~/.claude is the user's own file tree (no
  Full Disk Access needed), tmux is a unix socket, mDNS and HTTP are
  unprivileged. AppleScript injection (P3) is what would force a signed .app +
  SMAppService, and it is deliberately not here.

  __USER__ and __BIN__ are substituted by install.sh.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>io.teleport.tpd</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__BIN__</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Restart if it crashes, but not if it exits cleanly (a clean exit is
         an intentional stop, and respawning it would fight the user). -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <!--
      NO StandardOutPath. fld writes nothing to stdout under launchd (the one
      println! answers the version flag), and the path it used to name is now owned
      by the logger, which opens and ROTATES it. Two owners for one file is how
      a rotation renames a file the other one still holds open.

      StandardErrorPath stays, and its job narrowed: it captures what the logger
      cannot — a panic, a dyld failure, anything before logging starts.

      This file used to say it needed no rotation, because nothing writes to it
      in normal operation. That was true and was the trap: the abnormal case is
      a daemon that cannot start, which KeepAlive above restarts every ten
      seconds forever, each attempt appending its error before the logger is
      reached. The unrotated file grew fastest exactly when no daemon was
      running to rotate it. fld now bounds this file at startup
      (`logging::bound_foreign_log`) — renamed rather than truncated, since
      launchd owns the descriptor.
    -->
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__USER__/.teleport/tpd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
